    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29759" root="عفل" body-key="E">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَفَّلْتُهَا</span></b> , (O,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَعْفِيلٌ</span>, (O, K,) <i>I attributed to her the having what is termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَفَلٌ</span>. (O,
K. *) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَعْفِيلٌ</span> signifies also The <i>curing what
is termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَفَلٌ</span>. (Ibn-'Abbád, O, K.) One says,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عفّل المَرْأَةَ</span> <i>He cured the woman's</i> [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَفَل</span> or] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَفَلَة</span>.
(TK.)

